-- Nine Greens: mini golf for one to four players taking turns at one screen, on three
-- courses of nine holes each (a meadow, dunes and a lagoon) of banks, bumpers, sand, water,
-- wind and turning bars. Nothing but putting: no power-ups. The lowest total wins.
--
-- > cargo run --bin mira-play -- examples/nine_greens
--
-- Press 1 to 4, or click a number, for how many play, and then 1 to 3 for the course. On
-- your turn, hold the left mouse button on your ball and drag back, away from where it is
-- to go: the arrow shows the way, longer and redder the harder. Let go to putt, or let go where you began to take it back. Held anywhere
-- else and dragged, the view turns about the hole and tilts; so does a drag with the right
-- button, anywhere. The aim sways while it is held, more the harder the putt: let go when
-- it is on line. Or turn with A and D (or the arrows), tilt with W and S, hold Space, and
-- let go when the dots are long enough. On a phone, a finger does what the mouse does. A
-- ball in the water goes back to where it was hit from, a stroke added; seven strokes is the
-- most a hole takes.
--
-- Everything seen and heard is made here, from code: the holes from boxes and cylinders,
-- the letters pixel by pixel, the sounds sample by sample.

